  "findings": [
    "Exact derived run admits only bootstrap-exact-runtime, restore-complete-saved-inputs, actual-runtime-version and api-identity-census; each uses the qualified supervisor with 1200 seconds, and unknown routing labels reject before launch.",
    "The original exact runtime SHA, full qualified and failed-capture restoration, repeated input hashes, source rechecks, token removal during native execution, and read-only exact-source release reservation remain in the derived driver.",
    "Actual derived run/finally fixture covers success, partial native failure, malformed native failure, cleanup failure, final source failure and simultaneous body/cleanup failure. It requires the original exception object, all four commands, cleanup/heartbeat, restored supervisor globals, six terminal checks, complete output hashes and false repair/acceptance flags.",
    "capture_probe binds exact raw diagnostic bytes/hash before parsing; malformed partial native JSON remains in outputs and its terminal refusal does not replace the primary native failure. Complete diagnostic status alone does not waive outer failure.",
    "Actual transport fixtures are rebound to the derived namespace. They exercise both restoration failures and finally restoration of qualified paths/selected inputs, and exact publisher group/output arguments plus injected publication exception identity. The final publish_evidence transport call is explicitly mocked in those fixtures.",
    "The actual unchanged qualified publish_evidence/file-list bodies were inspected separately: attempt1, nonsymlink root/descendants, exact summary/parts verification, read-only release validation and reserved-only digest/no-clobber publication persist. It packs malformed nested diagnostic bytes without interpreting them as success.",
    "Actual source authorization fixtures retain disabled execution refusal before reservation/output, strict bool and paired read-only flags, exact input identity, fixed limits and forbidden routing/geometry/simulation/RC/acceptance flags.",
    "Template keeps contents/actions read at top, grants native publication write only, disables checkout credential persistence, requires controls before optional native, waits for exact-source reservation before dependencies, emits both complete control records and full failure artifacts, and always attempts publication."
  ],
